import{_ as a,o as r,c as t,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.BdWD-ld-.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"2026-11-16 · Agent Research and Competitive Intelligence","description":"Audit benchmarks, recovery receipts, enterprise authorization, employee collaboration and protocol interoperability; 39 observations and 6 analyses.","frontmatter":{"title":"2026-11-16 · Agent Research and Competitive Intelligence","description":"Audit benchmarks, recovery receipts, enterprise authorization, employee collaboration and protocol interoperability; 39 observations and 6 analyses."},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-16.md","filePath":"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-16.md","lastUpdated":1794794162000}'),i={name:"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-16.md"};function o(s,e,c,d,l,p){return r(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="_2026-11-16-·-agent-research-and-competitive-intelligence" tabindex="-1">2026-11-16 · Agent Research and Competitive Intelligence <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2026-11-16-·-agent-research-and-competitive-intelligence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2026-11-16 · Agent Research and Competitive Intelligence&quot;">​</a></h1><p>The main conclusion: <strong>digital-employee governance needs a checkable chain connecting authority, execution progress and acceptance.</strong> Yue Zhao released reproducible audit boards; Codex, Agents SDK, Paperclip and OpenHands tightened recovery/receipt boundaries; AG2 shipped ACP 1.0 and usage-accounting changes; MCP/A2A discussions emphasize independently observed effects and credible interoperability evidence. These are layered research leads, not demonstrated CodeFlowMu defects, local experiments or development-review conclusions.</p><p>Run date: <strong>2026-11-16, Asia/Shanghai</strong>. Execution start/event upper bound: <strong>2026-11-16T01:07:24Z (09:07:24 Beijing)</strong>. Last successful record: <strong>2026-11-14T065509Z</strong>. No successful Nov15 run was recorded; this run catches up from each source&#39;s successful/pending baseline without inventing a Nov15 report. Event dates and Z times below use <strong>UTC</strong>. Statuses reflect actual reads; changes after the event cutoff belong to subsequent runs.</p><h2 id="factual-observations" tabindex="-1">Factual observations <a class="header-anchor" href="#factual-observations" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Factual observations&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="o1-·-yue-zhao-reproducible-audit-leaderboards" tabindex="-1">O1 · Yue Zhao: reproducible audit leaderboards <a class="header-anchor" href="#o1-·-yue-zhao-reproducible-audit-leaderboards" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O1 · Yue Zhao: reproducible audit leaderboards&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-15 UTC。auditable v0.4.0 was RELEASED at 06:22Z: 44 PRE/LIVE/POST methods, six CatchBench boards with pinned populations/protocols, and golden checks. Oracles are unranked; skipped, errored or unchecked rows cannot silently pass. A flexible size control beats both GRADE dependency regressions on SWEGym but trails one on Tau, limiting general claims about structural superiority. Apache-2.0; full benchmarking requires datasets and optional dependencies. Zhao remains directly involved. Not reproduced locally.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/yzhao062/auditable/releases/tag/v0.4.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a></p><p>Worth discussing: how should GRADE gains be compared under size controls across datasets?</p><h3 id="o2-·-yue-zhao-review-round-and-worker-result-binding" tabindex="-1">O2 · Yue Zhao: review-round and worker-result binding <a class="header-anchor" href="#o2-·-yue-zhao-review-round-and-worker-result-binding" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O2 · Yue Zhao: review-round and worker-result binding&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-15 UTC。Two anywhere-agents main commits reject Gemini/Claude reviews containing only another round&#39;s marker (exit 70, publish nothing) and route Codex final messages to fresh result paths while preserving worker-written artifacts and nonzero exits. Exit zero without usable output also fails; fallback output is bounded. Marker checks do not prove semantic correctness. No new formal release was established.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/yzhao062/anywhere-agents/commit/db5707f837540785c22a26b109c658cd826457f6" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/yzhao062/anywhere-agents/commit/39525f4c96fdf83e4fb4b96e13cb44a8c0e6cb2e" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 2</a></p><p>Worth discussing: bind review round, artifact digest and task version rather than markers alone?</p><h3 id="o3-·-codex-remote-app-server-execution" tabindex="-1">O3 · Codex: remote app-server execution <a class="header-anchor" href="#o3-·-codex-remote-app-server-execution" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O3 · Codex: remote app-server execution&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-16 UTC。#61707 MERGED at 00:02Z: codex exec --remote connects to an existing app-server, creating or resuming a specified thread with remote configuration/credentials. Active threads, conflicting options and disconnection before completion have explicit failures. This is remote control/session continuation, not live-process migration; packaged release inclusion was not established.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/61707" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a></p><p>Worth discussing: how can a remote client retrieve authoritative receipts for unconfirmed work?</p><h3 id="o4-·-codex-tree-wide-budget-admission-and-attempt-accounting" tabindex="-1">O4 · Codex: tree-wide budget admission and attempt accounting <a class="header-anchor" href="#o4-·-codex-tree-wide-budget-admission-and-attempt-accounting" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O4 · Codex: tree-wide budget admission and attempt accounting&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-14–15 UTC。MERGED #61578/#61582 recheck shared budgets after approval/admission/lifecycle waits and before new MCP/model/tool work; exhausted trees stop automatic wakes. #61580 accounts synchronous MCP post-hook costs separately without retrying inference for invalid charges. #61587 adds stable request IDs and attempt numbers; #61581 uses neutral interruption markers. Consumed results remain; admission cannot undo effects. Release inclusion unverified.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/61578" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/61582" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 2</a> · <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/61580" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 3</a> · <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/61587" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 4</a> · <a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/61581" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 5</a></p><p>Worth discussing: align post-wait budget checks with effect settlement across the agent tree?</p><h3 id="o5-·-codex-environment-scoped-permission-descriptions" tabindex="-1">O5 · Codex: environment-scoped permission descriptions <a class="header-anchor" href="#o5-·-codex-environment-scoped-permission-descriptions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O5 · Codex: environment-scoped permission descriptions&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-14 UTC。#61494 MERGED: filesystem/network descriptions follow environment IDs, stale descriptions are withdrawn and shared requirements remain separate. The feature flag defaults OFF. This improves context accuracy; it is not evidence of new enforcement or default availability.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/61494" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a></p><p>Disposition: reference/ongoing observation; no immediate interaction proposed.</p><h3 id="o6-·-codex-visible-cloud-recovery-failures" tabindex="-1">O6 · Codex: visible Cloud recovery failures <a class="header-anchor" href="#o6-·-codex-visible-cloud-recovery-failures" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O6 · Codex: visible Cloud recovery failures&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-15 UTC。#61599 MERGED: Cloud recovery distinguishes missing conversations, access denial, changed/expired sign-in and exhausted reconnection, and cancels abandoned reads. The useful distinction is identity failure versus transient transport failure. Formal release inclusion remains unverified.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/61599" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a></p><p>Disposition: reference/ongoing observation; no immediate interaction proposed.</p><h3 id="o7-·-agents-python-checkpointed-patches-require-fresh-approval" tabindex="-1">O7 · Agents Python: checkpointed patches require fresh approval <a class="header-anchor" href="#o7-·-agents-python-checkpointed-patches-require-fresh-approval" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O7 · Agents Python: checkpointed patches require fresh approval&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-14 UTC。Native-preview #6008/#6003 MERGED: stop and join dispatch before snapshotting exact pending ApplyPatch IDs, retain completed sibling outputs, revalidate current declarations/action/owner and require fresh approval after restore. Lifecycle callbacks wait for approval. This is not automatic replay under stale grants; stable Python SDK release inclusion was not established.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6008" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6003" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 2</a></p><p>Worth discussing: expose traceable reapproval reasons after declaration/owner changes?</p><h3 id="o8-·-native-agents-python-js-receipts-exit-and-close-are-distinct" tabindex="-1">O8 · Native Agents Python/JS: receipts, exit and close are distinct <a class="header-anchor" href="#o8-·-native-agents-python-js-receipts-exit-and-close-are-distinct" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O8 · Native Agents Python/JS: receipts, exit and close are distinct&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-14–15 UTC。Python #5985/#5998/#6015/#6026 and JS #2662 MERGED: accepted manual replies stay accepted despite later budget failure; cancellation waits for owned remote commands to exit and reports unconfirmed cleanup while retiring connections. JS adds tool-search observations and current sandbox/editor binding checks. Corrected strict arguments still require approval; published alpha7 compatibility limits are documented. Native-preview merges, with some hosted/Docker verification pending.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/5985" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/5998" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 2</a> · <a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6015" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 3</a> · <a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6026" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 4</a> · <a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/2662" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 5</a></p><p>Worth discussing: distinguish replayable receipts for unconfirmed Stop and accepted replies?</p><h3 id="o9-·-paperclip-provider-started-turns-gain-runtime-behavior" tabindex="-1">O9 · Paperclip: provider-started turns gain runtime behavior <a class="header-anchor" href="#o9-·-paperclip-provider-started-turns-gain-runtime-behavior" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O9 · Paperclip: provider-started turns gain runtime behavior&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-14 UTC。#21612/#21456 MERGED: controller checkpoints recover waits for provider-started turns, and native ACPX Claude asks the Runner for them so background commands can outlive a turn without false finalization failures. This extends the previously reported contract into behavior on that adapter only. High learning value/high competitive risk; retain primary radar. Release inclusion unverified.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/21612" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/21456" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 2</a></p><p>Disposition: reference/ongoing observation; no immediate interaction proposed.</p><h3 id="o10-·-paperclip-recorded-tool-results-are-not-delivered-receipts" tabindex="-1">O10 · Paperclip: recorded tool results are not delivered receipts <a class="header-anchor" href="#o10-·-paperclip-recorded-tool-results-are-not-delivered-receipts" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O10 · Paperclip: recorded tool results are not delivered receipts&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-14–15 UTC。#21490 MERGED: an operationId envelope collision hid a recorded HTTP-200 result from OpenCode, leaving roughly 290 seconds pending and blocking later attach; results and closed-turn calls are now settled. #21786 preserves undispatched input for the next controller during restart detach instead of terminalizing it falsely. High learning/high risk; primary radar unchanged. These fixes do not prove end-to-end exactly-once.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/21490" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/21786" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 2</a></p><p>Worth discussing: distinguish recorded, delivered and effected outcomes during recovery?</p><h3 id="o11-·-paperclip-deployment-overlap-and-bounded-degraded-recovery" tabindex="-1">O11 · Paperclip: deployment overlap and bounded degraded recovery <a class="header-anchor" href="#o11-·-paperclip-deployment-overlap-and-bounded-degraded-recovery" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O11 · Paperclip: deployment overlap and bounded degraded recovery&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-15 UTC。#21697 MERGED: wait for a live outgoing owner before resuming its warm session, addressing two failures in eight prior release-swap cases. #21541 permits fresh-workspace continuation after permanent file loss without claiming file recovery; #21734 bounds repeated refused calls before fresh continuation. High learning/high risk. These are distinct degradation policies; upstream results are not local validation.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/21697" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/21541" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 2</a> · <a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/21734" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 3</a></p><p>Disposition: reference/ongoing observation; no immediate interaction proposed.</p><h3 id="o12-·-paperclip-fair-connection-admission-is-not-a-hard-cap" tabindex="-1">O12 · Paperclip: fair connection admission is not a hard cap <a class="header-anchor" href="#o12-·-paperclip-fair-connection-admission-is-not-a-hard-cap" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O12 · Paperclip: fair connection admission is not a hard cap&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-15 UTC。#21693 MERGED: dedicated database connections use FIFO admission with a default of 24, while nested/transactional paths bypass queues and timed-out waits can exceed it. The upstream burst reached 48, so 24 is not a hard connection cap. High learning/high risk; study recovery-burst fairness, latency and total connection budgets.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/21693" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a></p><p>Worth discussing: measure fairness and total connections when soft admission overshoots?</p><h3 id="o13-·-paperclip-scaling-harness-merged-thousand-agent-result-absent" tabindex="-1">O13 · Paperclip: scaling harness merged, thousand-agent result absent <a class="header-anchor" href="#o13-·-paperclip-scaling-harness-merged-thousand-agent-result-absent" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O13 · Paperclip: scaling harness merged, thousand-agent result absent&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-15 UTC。#21695 MERGED a real-agent ramp harness for 10/50/100/200/500/1000, queue/first-activity/latency/cost metrics, explicit missing-data markers, stop-on-failure and cleanup. It explicitly has not run against a real instance; earlier figures above 50 were modeled. High learning/high risk, but no demonstrated thousand-agent advantage; do not upgrade the maturity claim.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/21695" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a></p><p>Worth discussing: publish missing data, failures and cleanup evidence from the first real ramp?</p><h3 id="o14-·-openhands-forked-conversations-retain-decryptable-secret-state" tabindex="-1">O14 · OpenHands: forked conversations retain decryptable secret state <a class="header-anchor" href="#o14-·-openhands-forked-conversations-retain-decryptable-secret-state" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O14 · OpenHands: forked conversations retain decryptable secret state&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-15 UTC。#5765 MERGED: carry the source cipher and a deep-copied secrets registry through normal encrypted persistence so restarted forks can recover credentials. This fixes state inheritance, not authorization to share secrets across users. Upstream regression evidence only; release inclusion and local behavior unverified.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/5765" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a></p><p>Disposition: reference/ongoing observation; no immediate interaction proposed.</p><h3 id="o15-·-openhands-pid-reuse-does-not-prove-lease-ownership" tabindex="-1">O15 · OpenHands: PID reuse does not prove lease ownership <a class="header-anchor" href="#o15-·-openhands-pid-reuse-does-not-prove-lease-ownership" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O15 · OpenHands: PID reuse does not prove lease ownership&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-15 UTC。#6827 MERGED: local /proc start time disambiguates reused PIDs; zombie/dead owners can be reclaimed. Other hosts, legacy records, unavailable /proc and the same live process still follow existing TTL restrictions. This concerns Runtime ownership evidence, not automatic FCoP core requirements.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6827" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a></p><p>Worth discussing: expose owner-proof and TTL limitations without local /proc?</p><h3 id="o16-·-openhands-gateway-replies-must-reflect-the-current-run" tabindex="-1">O16 · OpenHands: gateway replies must reflect the current run <a class="header-anchor" href="#o16-·-openhands-gateway-replies-must-reflect-the-current-run" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O16 · OpenHands: gateway replies must reflect the current run&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-14 UTC。#6843 MERGED: a successful gateway run on a previously paused/errored conversation could return stale 409/500 status, prompting duplicate retries. The gateway now waits for its own live run while preserving genuine current-run errors. This separates historical state from current receipts; release inclusion unverified.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6843" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a></p><p>Disposition: reference/ongoing observation; no immediate interaction proposed.</p><h3 id="o17-·-openhands-total-timeout-budget-versus-fast-transient-failures" tabindex="-1">O17 · OpenHands: total timeout budget versus fast transient failures <a class="header-anchor" href="#o17-·-openhands-total-timeout-budget-versus-fast-transient-failures" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O17 · OpenHands: total timeout budget versus fast transient failures&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-15 UTC。#6822/#6866 MERGED: repeated long timeouts have an overall budget near twice the per-attempt timeout; the follow-up preserves quick transient retries and avoids mislabeling a quick final timeout as hard exhaustion. Configuration/settings errors are distinguished. Reading only the first PR would overstate termination behavior. Release inclusion unverified.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6822" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6866" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 2</a></p><p>Disposition: reference/ongoing observation; no immediate interaction proposed.</p><h3 id="o18-·-openhands-public-oauth-callbacks-and-app-consent-are-separate" tabindex="-1">O18 · OpenHands: public OAuth callbacks and App consent are separate <a class="header-anchor" href="#o18-·-openhands-public-oauth-callbacks-and-app-consent-are-separate" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O18 · OpenHands: public OAuth callbacks and App consent are separate&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-14–15 UTC。SDK #6221 MERGED public callbacks with one-use state, expiry/replay rejection and deployment prefixes; preregistered-client callback constraints still require configuration. Core #18572 MERGED current-revision, selected-secret consent for managed App enablement, with stop on withdrawal; install/mount alone never starts it. Authenticated public iframe flow remains unverified. These do not establish complete enterprise authorization.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6221" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/OpenHands/pull/18572" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 2</a></p><p>Disposition: reference/ongoing observation; no immediate interaction proposed.</p><h3 id="o19-·-openhands-windows-terminal-recovery-avoids-action-replay" tabindex="-1">O19 · OpenHands: Windows terminal recovery avoids action replay <a class="header-anchor" href="#o19-·-openhands-windows-terminal-recovery-avoids-action-replay" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O19 · OpenHands: Windows terminal recovery avoids action replay&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-15 UTC。#4962 MERGED PowerShell completion/error handling, private-console Ctrl-C and bounded descendant cleanup. Dead terminals may be recreated without replaying failed actions; packaged servers no longer assume system Python. Upstream Windows tests report 233 passes/196 skips, not local delivery acceptance. Directly relevant to Windows employee hosts.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/4962" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a></p><p>Disposition: reference/ongoing observation; no immediate interaction proposed.</p><h3 id="o20-·-browser-use-visual-judging-released-session-binding-fix-still-open" tabindex="-1">O20 · browser-use: visual judging released, session-binding fix still open <a class="header-anchor" href="#o20-·-browser-use-visual-judging-released-session-binding-fix-still-open" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O20 · browser-use: visual judging released, session-binding fix still open&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-14–16 UTC。RELEASED 1.0.5/1.0.6 add recent/final screenshots to same-model judging (#6403) and require trace-grounded, potentially empty gotchas (#6418). #6411 remains OPEN to fix final screenshots bound to the wrong session. Images are unredacted. Improved gotcha detection in 13 upstream runs did not improve task success; later trace rules have scripted tests, not paid-model evaluation. This is not independent acceptance.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/browser-use/browser-use/releases/tag/1.0.6" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/browser-use/browser-use/pull/6403" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 2</a> · <a href="https://github.com/browser-use/browser-use/pull/6418" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 3</a> · <a href="https://github.com/browser-use/browser-use/pull/6411" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 4</a></p><p>Worth discussing: bind screenshots to session, task version and an independent collector?</p><h3 id="o21-·-browser-use-default-model-changes-the-cost-contract" tabindex="-1">O21 · browser-use: default model changes the cost contract <a class="header-anchor" href="#o21-·-browser-use-default-model-changes-the-cost-contract" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O21 · browser-use: default model changes the cost contract&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-16 UTC。1.0.6 RELEASED at 00:51Z changes the default from bu-fast to high-reasoning bu-4.0 (#6430). Release notes list input/output prices rising from $0.12/$0.60 to $1.80/$9 per million tokens, a 15x unit-price increase; one example is not a universal task-cost ratio. Explicit bu-fast retains the prior choice. Long-running employees need pinned model/reasoning/pricing assumptions.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/browser-use/browser-use/releases/tag/1.0.6" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/browser-use/browser-use/pull/6430" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 2</a></p><p>Disposition: reference/ongoing observation; no immediate interaction proposed.</p><h3 id="o22-·-browser-use-governance-stack-remains-draft" tabindex="-1">O22 · browser-use: governance stack remains draft <a class="header-anchor" href="#o22-·-browser-use-governance-stack-remains-draft" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O22 · browser-use: governance stack remains draft&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-15–16 UTC。#6414/#6416/#6415/#6421/#6417 are OPEN+DRAFT: action hooks, effect-point approval, redacted hash-chain logs, strict domains and least-privilege login copying. Cell hooks are not universal effect boundaries; post-action log failures may only be logged; valid chains do not prove completeness; strict domains omit WebSocket/WebRTC/WebTransport and raw-socket routes. Research proposals, not shipped governance.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/browser-use/browser-use/pull/6414" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/browser-use/browser-use/pull/6416" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 2</a> · <a href="https://github.com/browser-use/browser-use/pull/6415" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 3</a> · <a href="https://github.com/browser-use/browser-use/pull/6421" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 4</a> · <a href="https://github.com/browser-use/browser-use/pull/6417" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 5</a></p><p>Worth discussing: use route inventories and external anchors to detect omissions, not only chain validity?</p><h3 id="o23-·-adk-adaptive-team-orchestration-is-experimental" tabindex="-1">O23 · ADK: adaptive team orchestration is experimental <a class="header-anchor" href="#o23-·-adk-adaptive-team-orchestration-is-experimental" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O23 · ADK: adaptive team orchestration is experimental&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-15 UTC。#8174 is OPEN, non-draft: a Python workflow coordinates specialist rosters, TaskPlan/RoundAssessment, bounded stalls/replanning/rounds and optional human plan review. Session snapshots and stable call IDs support continuation; new user input resets it. Mock/feature tests only, no hosted-model/manual E2E acceptance. A candidate for studying delegation, replacement and coordination costs, not a released team product.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/google/adk-python/pull/8174" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a></p><p>Worth discussing: count replanning, human reviews and late specialist outputs in coordination cost?</p><h3 id="o24-·-adk-mcp-continuity-needs-application-identity" tabindex="-1">O24 · ADK: MCP continuity needs application identity <a class="header-anchor" href="#o24-·-adk-mcp-continuity-needs-application-identity" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O24 · ADK: MCP continuity needs application identity&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-15 UTC。#8164 is OPEN, non-draft: an explicit session_id can continue conversations across MCP connections, unknown IDs create sessions and hosts own lifecycle. The handle is not a credential: anyone knowing it can join under the proposal. For FCoP interoperation this supplies correlation; identity/tenant authorization must be separately enforced.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/google/adk-python/pull/8164" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a></p><p>Worth discussing: bind session handles to authenticated principals and tenants?</p><h3 id="o25-·-crewai-fail-closed-hooks-remain-unmerged" tabindex="-1">O25 · CrewAI: fail-closed hooks remain unmerged <a class="header-anchor" href="#o25-·-crewai-fail-closed-hooks-remain-unmerged" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O25 · CrewAI: fail-closed hooks remain unmerged&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-15 UTC。#9465 is OPEN, non-draft: optional on_error=abort raises HookAborted on pre/post-tool hook errors and can keep unprocessed output from reaching the model. The default remains fail-open. Focused tests are not merged capability. The key question is how a post-hook refusal accounts for an already-performed external effect.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/pull/9465" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a></p><p>Worth discussing: settle an already-performed effect when a post-hook aborts?</p><h3 id="o26-·-orkas-upgrade-and-diagnostic-boundaries" tabindex="-1">O26 · Orkas: upgrade and diagnostic boundaries <a class="header-anchor" href="#o26-·-orkas-upgrade-and-diagnostic-boundaries" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O26 · Orkas: upgrade and diagnostic boundaries&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-15 UTC。#220/#219 MERGED physical-path checks for managed upgrade copy/unlink operations and linked ancestors, atomic activation/retry, and redaction of escaped/truncated credentials. Upstream tests are not full Windows installer acceptance or proof of universal secret-free logging. High learning value/medium competitive risk; keep primary radar and study employee delivery/diagnostics.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/Orkas-AI/Orkas/pull/220" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/Orkas-AI/Orkas/pull/219" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 2</a></p><p>Disposition: reference/ongoing observation; no immediate interaction proposed.</p><h3 id="o27-·-paradev-phone-initiated-cross-host-workspace-moves" tabindex="-1">O27 · Paradev: phone-initiated cross-host workspace moves <a class="header-anchor" href="#o27-·-paradev-phone-initiated-cross-host-workspace-moves" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O27 · Paradev: phone-initiated cross-host workspace moves&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-14 UTC。The original Superset repository redirects to ParadevAI/Paradev; preserve that provenance. #9612/#9732 MERGED durable, source-host-owned move IDs initiated by phone and roster/relay moves from another computer to cloud. Feature flags and source/destination prerequisites apply; real multi-host manual acceptance is pending. MIT; high learning/high risk. Retain primary radar and emphasize mobile operations, without claiming seamless live-process migration.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/ParadevAI/Paradev/pull/9612" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/ParadevAI/Paradev/pull/9732" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 2</a></p><p>Worth discussing: what are terminal query/cancellation semantics after phone/source-host disconnection?</p><h3 id="o28-·-paradev-background-subagents-and-continued-dialogue" tabindex="-1">O28 · Paradev: background subagents and continued dialogue <a class="header-anchor" href="#o28-·-paradev-background-subagents-and-continued-dialogue" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O28 · Paradev: background subagents and continued dialogue&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-14 UTC。#9733 MERGED: background subagents no longer block the parent dialogue; late results join the latest turn, while foreground work still queues. The implementation pins protocol v1 after a v2 steering case produced roughly 48 seconds of duplicate replies. Protocol upgrades are not automatically improvements. High learning/high risk; retain primary radar and study ownership of late artifacts.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/ParadevAI/Paradev/pull/9733" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a></p><p>Worth discussing: prevent late child outputs from attaching to a superseding plan?</p><h3 id="o29-·-orca-reclaiming-phone-control-and-sleep-recovery" tabindex="-1">O29 · Orca: reclaiming phone control and sleep recovery <a class="header-anchor" href="#o29-·-orca-reclaiming-phone-control-and-sleep-recovery" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O29 · Orca: reclaiming phone control and sleep recovery&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-15–16 UTC。#42785/#42864 MERGED: Take back all reclaims phone-driven browsers and terminals; a saved Codex session survives wake-then-sleep by forgetting an old exit only at the correct replacement spawn. Full dependency/build/test validation was not run upstream for the latter. High learning/medium-high risk; retain second circle with more attention to human takeover. Separately, v1.4.259 was RELEASED Nov14 at 21:20Z with workspace cleanup controls and focused subagent live-step/final-answer views; this does not establish that the later PRs were in that version.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/42785" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/42864" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 2</a> · <a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/releases/tag/v1.4.259" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 3</a></p><p>Disposition: reference/ongoing observation; no immediate interaction proposed.</p><h3 id="o30-·-agentlas-four-memory-scopes-introduce-migration-constraints" tabindex="-1">O30 · Agentlas: four memory scopes introduce migration constraints <a class="header-anchor" href="#o30-·-agentlas-four-memory-scopes-introduce-migration-constraints" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O30 · Agentlas: four memory scopes introduce migration constraints&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-15 UTC。RELEASED os-v1.2.98 at 13:42Z adds personal/agent/project/session scopes, owner-bound recall/forgetting, unique project IDs, carried unfinished forgets and explicit partial reads. Session-end hooks record without starting a model. Desktop initiates one-time conversion; update the engine first, since old engines disable schema-2 memory. Apache-2.0; high learning/medium risk, retain second circle with more memory-governance attention. Not installed locally; some host/Windows sessions remain unverified.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/agentlas-ai/Agentlas-OS/releases/tag/os-v1.2.98" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a></p><p>Worth discussing: verify owner-scoped forgetting and distinguish partial reads from empty memory?</p><h3 id="o31-·-vibe-kanban-new-delivery-does-not-establish-a-business-revival" tabindex="-1">O31 · Vibe Kanban: new delivery does not establish a business revival <a class="header-anchor" href="#o31-·-vibe-kanban-new-delivery-does-not-establish-a-business-revival" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O31 · Vibe Kanban: new delivery does not establish a business revival&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-15 UTC。RELEASED v0.1.46.1794744340 at 13:16Z packages previously observed ACP registry/approval-bridge work, pins Codex with valid macOS signing and disables analytics/crash reports. The increment is formal delivery, not new versions of old PR facts. Medium learning/low current risk; retain low-frequency post-sunset/failed-business observation. This release does not establish commercial revival.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/BloopAI/vibe-kanban/releases/tag/v0.1.46.1794744340" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a></p><p>Disposition: reference/ongoing observation; no immediate interaction proposed.</p><h3 id="o32-·-mcp-approval-evidence-and-observed-effects-are-being-separated" tabindex="-1">O32 · MCP: approval evidence and observed effects are being separated <a class="header-anchor" href="#o32-·-mcp-approval-evidence-and-observed-effects-are-being-separated" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O32 · MCP: approval evidence and observed effects are being separated&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-15–16 UTC。SEP #2848 remains OPEN+DRAFT. New comments, not an adopted protocol revision, discuss named call digests, separate decision/effect/route coverage, and why approval cannot settle outcome-unknown. A commenter reports a truncated chain still verifying and argues for external completeness anchors and independent observers; an OAC participant distinguishes executor receipts from independent effects. These are proposals/upstream claims, not local results; the official-SDK reference prerequisite remains unmet.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/pull/2848#issuecomment-6887019800" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/pull/2848#issuecomment-6888074338" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 2</a> · <a href="https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/pull/2848#issuecomment-6903646262" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 3</a></p><p>Worth discussing: cross-check canonical digests and one-decision/two-effect negative vectors?</p><h3 id="o33-·-a2a-extension-independent-evidence-corrected-mixed-fault-vectors-added" tabindex="-1">O33 · A2A extension: independent evidence corrected, mixed-fault vectors added <a class="header-anchor" href="#o33-·-a2a-extension-independent-evidence-corrected-mixed-fault-vectors-added" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O33 · A2A extension: independent evidence corrected, mixed-fault vectors added&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-14–15 UTC。A2A #2028 stays OPEN; third-party VAID #176 MERGED at 20:19Z on Nov15, adding vectors 15–18: invalid signatures precede incomplete-chain checks; absent optional VAID is not automatically denied. The README corrects reference-verifier reproductions mislabeled as independent implementations; independent evidence covers only 01–06. Reference 18/18 is neither two independent full implementations nor A2A-core adoption.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/a2aproject/A2A/issues/2028#issuecomment-6896207423" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/solara-associates/vaid/pull/176" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 2</a></p><p>Worth discussing: independently implement the new mixed-fault vectors and separate reproduction evidence?</p><h3 id="o34-·-mcp-cached-tool-schemas-need-compatibility-rules" tabindex="-1">O34 · MCP: cached tool schemas need compatibility rules <a class="header-anchor" href="#o34-·-mcp-cached-tool-schemas-need-compatibility-rules" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O34 · MCP: cached tool schemas need compatibility rules&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-15 UTC。#3554 was opened and remains OPEN: its author reports Claude Code/ChatGPT rejecting results against cached outputSchema after required fields were removed. list_changed cannot eliminate refresh races. The suggested note favors optional additions and retaining replaced fields. This is a user report/non-normative proposal, not a universal client result or adopted specification.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/issues/3554" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a></p><p>Worth discussing: carry schema versions/digests to distinguish upgrade races from invalid results?</p><h3 id="o35-·-mcp-an-unambiguous-issuer-is-not-a-verified-issuer" tabindex="-1">O35 · MCP: an unambiguous issuer is not a verified issuer <a class="header-anchor" href="#o35-·-mcp-an-unambiguous-issuer-is-not-a-verified-issuer" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O35 · MCP: an unambiguous issuer is not a verified issuer&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-14 UTC。Python SDK #3850 stays OPEN. New comments correct that issuer already exists and is checked before token exchange; the remaining question is credentials following resource-chosen endpoints when issuer is omitted. Rejecting multiple servers removes ambiguity, not single-server provenance risk. The report spans FastMCP versions and SDK main; it is not evidence that all MCP deployments leak credentials. Backport/default-path documentation remain unresolved.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/issues/3850#issuecomment-6877514411" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/python-sdk/issues/3850#issuecomment-6881273787" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 2</a></p><p>Worth discussing: retain single-issuer/no-issuer negative cases with backport documentation?</p><h3 id="o36-·-langfuse-unifying-session-and-api-policy-authorization" tabindex="-1">O36 · Langfuse: unifying session and API policy authorization <a class="header-anchor" href="#o36-·-langfuse-unifying-session-and-api-policy-authorization" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O36 · Langfuse: unifying session and API policy authorization&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-14–16 UTC。#20235 is OPEN, non-draft: Web/tRPC sessions would share policy authorization with the public API and audit role IDs; all production regions must pass role-drift checks before merge. Costs include a query per session read, policies in client session payloads and mixed historical audit formats. DB/preview acceptance is incomplete. This is a governance migration candidate, not shipped unified authorization.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/langfuse/langfuse/pull/20235" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a></p><p>Worth discussing: verify UI/API parity and revocation against existing sessions?</p><h3 id="o37-·-swe-agent-completed-artifacts-and-evaluation-indexes-are-distinct" tabindex="-1">O37 · SWE-agent: completed artifacts and evaluation indexes are distinct <a class="header-anchor" href="#o37-·-swe-agent-completed-artifacts-and-evaluation-indexes-are-distinct" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O37 · SWE-agent: completed artifacts and evaluation indexes are distinct&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-15 UTC。#1642 is OPEN, non-draft: reconstruct missing/truncated .pred files from explicit trajectory submissions, including null patches, then atomically publish while preserving permissions/ACLs for concurrent evaluators. Upstream reproduction and 32 focused tests are reported; no local validation or merge. The research question is verifiable recovery when artifacts exist but derived delivery indexes are lost.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/SWE-agent/SWE-agent/pull/1642" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a></p><p>Worth discussing: bind reconstructed prediction indexes to task revision and independent acceptance?</p><h3 id="o38-·-ag2-1-3-2-multi-question-decisions-usage-semantics-and-acp-migration" tabindex="-1">O38 · AG2 1.3.2: multi-question decisions, usage semantics and ACP migration <a class="header-anchor" href="#o38-·-ag2-1-3-2-multi-question-decisions-usage-semantics-and-acp-migration" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O38 · AG2 1.3.2: multi-question decisions, usage semantics and ACP migration&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-15 UTC。v1.3.2 RELEASED at 16:37Z combines flat-schema multi-question decisions with pre-request rejection of unsupported schemas; normalized cache/thinking-token usage can reach budgets earlier without rewriting historical records. ACP extras now require &gt;=1,&lt;2, dropping 0.12, separating messages from final answers and preserving resource/tool structures; queued input moves to the next turn instead of overwriting final/client handoffs. Python 3.15 is supported but Windows PyYAML source builds may need a compiler. Shipped interoperability/cost contracts, not locally upgrade-tested.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/ag2ai/ag2/releases/tag/v1.3.2" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a></p><p>Worth discussing: avoid double-counted cache usage across historical/new accounting versions?</p><h3 id="o39-·-langchain-provider-packages-add-gateway-routing-and-change-python-support" tabindex="-1">O39 · LangChain: provider packages add gateway routing and change Python support <a class="header-anchor" href="#o39-·-langchain-provider-packages-add-gateway-routing-and-change-python-support" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O39 · LangChain: provider packages add gateway routing and change Python support&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Event date: 2026-11-15 UTC。RELEASED langchain-xai 1.4.0, langchain-mistralai 1.2.0 and langchain-groq 1.2.0 add LangSmith gateway routing; their notes also remove Python 3.10 support in the partner packages, with reasoning-stream fixes in Mistral. These are multi-provider integration/delivery leads, not proof of enterprise credential isolation or audit completeness. Local migration unverified.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain/releases/tag/langchain-xai%3D%3D1.4.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 1</a> · <a href="https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain/releases/tag/langchain-mistralai%3D%3D1.2.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 2</a> · <a href="https://github.com/langchain-ai/langchain/releases/tag/langchain-groq%3D%3D1.2.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence 3</a></p><p>Disposition: reference/ongoing observation; no immediate interaction proposed.</p><h2 id="research-analysis" tabindex="-1">Research analysis <a class="header-anchor" href="#research-analysis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Research analysis&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="a1-·-first-experiment-candidate-settle-unknown-outcomes-before-retrying" tabindex="-1">A1 · First experiment candidate: settle unknown outcomes before retrying <a class="header-anchor" href="#a1-·-first-experiment-candidate-settle-unknown-outcomes-before-retrying" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A1 · First experiment candidate: settle unknown outcomes before retrying&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Based on: <strong>O2</strong>、<strong>O7</strong>、<strong>O8</strong>、<strong>O9</strong>、<strong>O10</strong>、<strong>O11</strong>、<strong>O15</strong>、<strong>O16</strong>、<strong>O19</strong>、<strong>O37</strong>。</p><p>Supported: independent projects distinguish acceptance, launch, persistence, delivery and ownership, but their scoped fixes do not establish exactly-once. Hypothesis: CodeFlowMu recovery across PM/workers, host restart or model changes may need independently checkable effects before retry, without a demonstrated local defect. Candidate: an isolated fake write tool with occurrence IDs; cut connectivity after acceptance, after effect and before receipt, restart/change workers, and inspect counts/ownership/delivery through an independent reader. Require no duplicate effect, honest unknown outcomes, no stale artifact overwrite and no writes from fenced owners. Costs include durable receipts, fencing and provider queries; unqueryable effects remain unknown. Compare FCoP task/artifact/evidence correlation separately from Runtime leases/cancellation. Proposed, not run.</p><h3 id="a2-·-first-experiment-candidate-make-audit-and-acceptance-falsifiable" tabindex="-1">A2 · First experiment candidate: make audit and acceptance falsifiable <a class="header-anchor" href="#a2-·-first-experiment-candidate-make-audit-and-acceptance-falsifiable" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A2 · First experiment candidate: make audit and acceptance falsifiable&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Based on: <strong>O1</strong>、<strong>O2</strong>、<strong>O20</strong>、<strong>O22</strong>、<strong>O32</strong>、<strong>O33</strong>、<strong>O34</strong>、<strong>O37</strong>。</p><p>Supported: goldens/size controls constrain audit claims; screenshots can bind to the wrong session, same-model judging is not independent, hash chains do not establish completeness and reference reproductions are not independent implementations. Hypothesis: employee acceptance should bind artifact task/version, approval and independently observed effect. Candidate: pin auditable 0.4.0 and reproduce affordable golden tasks, then inject wrong-session screenshots, stale artifacts, truncated logs, stale schemas, one decision/two effects and executor-only claims. Measure false acceptance, unknowns, localization, cost and size controls while retaining skipped/errors. FCoP research concerns artifact digests/versions/evidence references; external log anchors belong to deployment. Full graph dependencies are costly, so start lightweight. Not installed or benchmarked; experiment candidate.</p><h3 id="a3-·-mechanism-to-study-action-bound-approval-with-current-authorization" tabindex="-1">A3 · Mechanism to study: action-bound approval with current authorization <a class="header-anchor" href="#a3-·-mechanism-to-study-action-bound-approval-with-current-authorization" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A3 · Mechanism to study: action-bound approval with current authorization&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Based on: <strong>O5</strong>、<strong>O7</strong>、<strong>O14</strong>、<strong>O18</strong>、<strong>O22</strong>、<strong>O24</strong>、<strong>O25</strong>、<strong>O32</strong>、<strong>O33</strong>、<strong>O35</strong>、<strong>O36</strong>。</p><p>Supported: checkpoint reapproval, current-revision secret consent, issuer binding and Web/API policy alignment avoid treating stale context as current authority. Hypothesis: roles/delegation describe duties; execution must also bind current principal/tool/target/arguments/environment. Candidate: change tenant, declarations, App revision, issuer, target or credentials after approval, and restart while waiting; require rejection/reapproval while retaining valid positive controls. Compare portable authorization/evidence references and denial semantics at FCoP level; secret custody, coverage and enforcement points at adapter/Runtime level; UI/API parity at product level. Costs include queries, invalidation and compatibility. Draft hooks and unmerged Langfuse remain proposals. Ongoing observation/experiment candidate, not validated.</p><h3 id="a4-·-experience-candidates-teams-late-results-and-scoped-memory" tabindex="-1">A4 · Experience candidates: teams, late results and scoped memory <a class="header-anchor" href="#a4-·-experience-candidates-teams-late-results-and-scoped-memory" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A4 · Experience candidates: teams, late results and scoped memory&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Based on: <strong>O2</strong>、<strong>O23</strong>、<strong>O27</strong>、<strong>O28</strong>、<strong>O29</strong>、<strong>O30</strong>、<strong>O38</strong>。</p><p>Supported: ADK proposes bounded replanning, Paradev accepts background results, Agentlas ships scoped memory and AG2 batches decisions sharing input; none proves general team efficiency. Hypothesis: persistent employees need stable role/project identity and versioned handoff state without mixing personal/project memory. Experience candidates: Agentlas standalone memory (Apache-2.0), AG2 1.3.2 and separately Paradev (MIT); inspect ADK before treating it as runnable accepted capability. Use same-name projects, two users in one role, late child outputs, human plan edits and stalled loops; measure correct delivery, coordination tokens, interventions and completed forgetting. Costs include host compatibility, migration and identity mapping. No local installation. FCoP covers task/artifact versions and handoffs, not automatically memory engines/scheduling.</p><h3 id="a5-·-research-priority-budgets-recovery-load-and-delivery-costs" tabindex="-1">A5 · Research priority: budgets, recovery load and delivery costs <a class="header-anchor" href="#a5-·-research-priority-budgets-recovery-load-and-delivery-costs" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A5 · Research priority: budgets, recovery load and delivery costs&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Based on: <strong>O4</strong>、<strong>O6</strong>、<strong>O12</strong>、<strong>O13</strong>、<strong>O17</strong>、<strong>O19</strong>、<strong>O21</strong>、<strong>O26</strong>、<strong>O31</strong>、<strong>O38</strong>、<strong>O39</strong>。</p><p>Supported: Codex separates admission/accounting; Paperclip&#39;s 24 is soft and its scaling harness is unrun; browser-use changes default prices; AG2 normalizes cache/thinking usage; Python support changes affect Windows installs. Hypothesis: simultaneous employee recovery amplifies connection, budget, approval and diagnostic costs. Candidate: affordable 5/20-worker recovery ramps with pinned models/prices and injected exhaustion, slow connections, timeouts and upgrade failure. Measure p95 continuation/first activity, peak connections, costs and lost/duplicate work; missing data stays missing. Compare usage/state facts at protocol level, admission fairness/budgets/dependencies at Runtime/delivery level. Retain Orkas upgrades and Vibe signing as references, not local maturity proof.</p><h3 id="a6-·-radar-and-protocol-judgment-mobile-governance-and-versioned-interoperability" tabindex="-1">A6 · Radar and protocol judgment: mobile governance and versioned interoperability <a class="header-anchor" href="#a6-·-radar-and-protocol-judgment-mobile-governance-and-versioned-interoperability" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A6 · Radar and protocol judgment: mobile governance and versioned interoperability&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Based on: <strong>O3</strong>、<strong>O8</strong>、<strong>O9</strong>、<strong>O18</strong>、<strong>O24</strong>、<strong>O27</strong>、<strong>O28</strong>、<strong>O29</strong>、<strong>O31</strong>、<strong>O32</strong>、<strong>O33</strong>、<strong>O34</strong>、<strong>O38</strong>。</p><p>Supported: Paradev durable moves, Orca takeback and Codex remote span product operations, control ownership and remote execution. AG2&#39;s breaking ACP1 migration and Paradev&#39;s v1 fallback show protocol names do not guarantee capability parity. Hypothesis: study phone approval/evidence/pause/takeover/disconnected queries rather than shrinking desktop UI. Compare FCoP separately with MCP tool calls, ACP host sessions and A2A cross-agent tasks/delegation; VAID/OAC are third-party approaches, not official same-layer replacements. Candidate: a pinned-version start/accept/pause/cancel/resume/artifact matrix checking state, events, receipts, identity and evidence loss. Keep Paperclip/Paradev high-risk primary, Orkas primary, Orca/Agentlas specialist second circle, Vibe low-frequency. No local experiment or development assignment.</p><h2 id="cross-project-resonance-and-disposition" tabindex="-1">Cross-project resonance and disposition <a class="header-anchor" href="#cross-project-resonance-and-disposition" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Cross-project resonance and disposition&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Within the inspected projects, recovery distinguishes acceptance, execution, effect and delivery; governance spans approval, credentials, memory, artifacts and takeover; benchmarks, hash chains and screenshots need negative controls. Similar fixes do not establish a universal result.</p><p>Prioritize A1 unknown-outcome settlement and A2 independent acceptance as experiment candidates; retain A3 current-authorization revalidation next. Agentlas/AG2/Paradev in A4 are uninstalled experience candidates; A5 is an affordable recovery measurement candidate; A6 proposes pinned-version interoperability cases. <strong>This monitoring run performed 0 local experiments, 0 articles, 0 development reviews, 0 development assignments and 0 external comments.</strong> These describe this monitoring stage only and do not alter Runtime lifecycle facts. Technical discussion topics are recorded per observation; drafts/receipts remain local. No comments or stars were posted in this run.</p><p>Radar summary: Paperclip/Paradev have high learning value/high risk and remain primary; Orkas high learning/medium risk remains primary; Orca high learning/medium-high risk and Agentlas high learning/medium risk remain specialist second-circle targets; Vibe stays medium learning/low risk, low-frequency post-sunset delivery observation. No local evaluation establishes enterprise maturity.</p><h2 id="dual-source-verification-and-coverage" tabindex="-1">Dual-source verification and coverage <a class="header-anchor" href="#dual-source-verification-and-coverage" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Dual-source verification and coverage&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>The connected GitHub tool read Registry on latest main first: <strong>47 researchers</strong>, with repositories as evidence entrances. All runbook projects/radar targets were retained: 88 original repository entries, 264 initial commits/issues/releases queries; 180 query windows complete, 78 pagination-incomplete and 6 inaccessible/redirected. Five correct follow-up page/redirect queries and selected PR/issue/comment/document reads supplement them. Completing an API window does not exhaust a source&#39;s channels.</li><li>Paperclip/Orca commit page 2 remained full, so their pending windows remain and complete baselines do not advance; full issue/release pages also stay pending. The original Superset route redirects; recent original Paradev events were checked without claiming all historical gaps closed. TSA returned three API 404s; access failure is not proof of shutdown.</li><li>All six additional governance researchers&#39; designated GitHub entrances were queried. Mansura Habiba&#39;s bulbasaur-skill-cli remains a related project, not AGENTSAFE&#39;s official artifact. Other relationships follow the boundary document. Zhao&#39;s supplemental sources retain original provenance and are not automatically official paper implementations. Zhao, Paperclip&#39;s nickyleach/cryppadotta and OpenHands&#39; neubig/enyst remain directly involved in inspected commits/PRs; maintainer identity auditing was not exhaustive.</li><li>Non-GitHub checks separately covered <a href="https://prod.cursor.com/en-US/changelog" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Cursor&#39;s official changelog</a>, <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/engineering" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Anthropic engineering</a>, <a href="https://www.langchain.com/blog" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">LangChain&#39;s blog</a>, <a href="https://docs.ag2.ai/docs/blog" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">AG2&#39;s blog</a>, <a href="https://yzhao062.github.io/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Zhao&#39;s homepage</a> and confirmed pages for Kaptein, Agrawal, de Witt, Shaokun Zhang and Haoyu Wang. No sufficiently verified new non-GitHub event qualified in this window; Nov13/older material remains previously reported/history. DART (Sep30) and SafeClaw-R (Mar28) are not today&#39;s papers. Selected X searches do not exhaust 47 researchers&#39; accounts/replies; Mansura&#39;s independent social entrance was not fully checked.</li><li>Primary GitHub evidence can support engineering facts independently; two GitHub links are not two source types. README/license/business boundaries were deeply read for selected experience targets only. Roadmap/discussions, all architecture/install documents and every author&#39;s social stream remain incompletely covered. Only fully successful source queries advance local baselines; partial, inaccessible and unchecked statuses remain distinct.</li></ul><p>Daily intelligence remains separate from Research Runtime. Chinese/English share observation/analysis IDs, states, sources and judgments. Deployment receipts and actual live clicks are recorded separately: committing source is not online completion, and deployment/verification failures must be reported in chat.</p>',186)])])}const g=a(i,[["render",o]]);export{h as __pageData,g as default};
